            0.606
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "People using the Roman system made use of a calculating tool called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "abacus",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to perform their arithmetic operations. We will see what it is in a later section. However, only specially trained people used this tool for calculation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.605,
            0.849,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "While going through the number systems discussed above, it should not be understood that, historically, one system developed as an improvement over the previous system. This point should be kept in mind when studying the upcoming number systems too. The actual story of how each of the number systems developed is much more complex, and many times not clearly known, and so we will not try to trace this in the chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.745,
            0.293,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.77,
            0.801,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A group of indigenous people in a Pacific island use different sequences of number names to count different objects. Why do you think they do this?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
